{
  "info": {
    "name": "Day 18 — Kafka store",
    "description": "The same store with Kafka as the event log. Every event goes to the `orders` topic, keyed by order id.\n\n1. `npm run infra:up` (Kafka + UI, creates the topic), then `npm run dev:all` (orders, inventory, notifications). Start `npm run analytics` when you get to that folder.\n2. **Place an order** saves the new order id into `orderId`, so **Pay** and **Ship** act on it — all three land in the same partition.\n3. Kafka UI: http://localhost:8085. Consumer groups and lag in the terminal: `npm run groups`.\n\nSKUs: SKU-1 keyboard $49, SKU-2 mouse $25, SKU-3 mug $12. An empty body places a default order.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "ordersUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4301"
    },
    {
      "key": "inventoryUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4302"
    },
    {
      "key": "notificationsUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4303"
    },
    {
      "key": "analyticsUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4304"
    },
    {
      "key": "orderId",
      "value": "ord-1001"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. One order's events (ordering by key)",
      "description": "Run these three in order. Each response shows the partition and offset — the same partition every time.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Place an order (OrderPlaced)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{ordersUrl}}/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{ordersUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Publishes OrderPlaced keyed by the new order id, and saves that id into {{orderId}}.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"customer\": \"alice@shop.com\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"sku\": \"SKU-1\",\n      \"qty\": 1\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"orderId\", pm.response.json().order.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Pay for it (OrderPaid)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{ordersUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/pay",
              "host": [
                "{{ordersUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "{{orderId}}",
                "pay"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same key, so the same partition as the OrderPlaced event."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Ship it (OrderShipped)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{ordersUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/ship",
              "host": [
                "{{ordersUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "{{orderId}}",
                "ship"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Notifications logs placed → paid → shipped, in order."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{ordersUrl}}/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{ordersUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Orders this process created, with their current status."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Lag",
      "description": "Start analytics slowly (`SLOW_MS=100 npm run analytics`), send the burst, then watch the analytics group's lag climb and drain in the Kafka UI or `npm run groups`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Burst of 150 orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{ordersUrl}}/orders/burst",
              "host": [
                "{{ordersUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "burst"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Publishes that many OrderPlaced events at once.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"count\": 150\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. What each consumer group did",
      "description": "Each service is its own consumer group, so each one reads every event.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Stock levels (group: inventory)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{inventoryUrl}}/inventory",
              "host": [
                "{{inventoryUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "inventory"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Stock per SKU on this copy. Extra copies (PORT=4312 …) split the partitions and keep their own counts."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Emails sent (group: notifications)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{notificationsUrl}}/notifications",
              "host": [
                "{{notificationsUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "notifications"
              ]
            },
            "description": "One email per event, with the partition and offset it came from."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Analytics totals (group: analytics)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{analyticsUrl}}/analytics",
              "host": [
                "{{analyticsUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "analytics"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Revenue and counts. Started late, it still reads the topic from offset 0. After `npm run reset-offsets -- analytics`, a restart replays the full history."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Is each service up?",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{ordersUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{ordersUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Inventory",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{inventoryUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{inventoryUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Notifications",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{notificationsUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{notificationsUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Analytics",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{analyticsUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{analyticsUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Only answers once `npm run analytics` is running."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
